Middleware chain Tag(Filter(pagerHandler)) built by Chain (a slice of
func(Handler) Handler) and called through the interface. Under Go
semantics: ErrPager and core.ErrDropped, each wrapped once by "%s: %w".
VTA is context-insensitive: every closure converted to HandlerFunc is a
Candidate of the adapter's f(e), so the accepted result is the set of
hf_handle_decl (all middleware Origins and wraps, even main.errQuota,
whose closure never enters a chain). It must contain ErrPager and
ErrDropped under "%s: %w". The Recover closure shows up as
unresolved(memory) with span "-" (see recover_lit).
-- args --
-chain-depth=1 main.go:@pipeline
